# 6. Model Development (5-Fold CV Models)

These models use **5-fold cross-validation** as specified.

## 6.1 Model 4: k-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) Regression

KNN is a non-parametric method that predicts based on the average of the k nearest training observations. It requires scaled features for optimal performance.

### 6.1.1 Model Training with Hyperparameter Tuning

```{r knn-model}
# Define tuning grid for k (number of neighbors)
knn_grid <- expand.grid(
  k = c(1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 15, 20, 25, 30)
)

# Train KNN model using scaled data
knn_model <- train(
  ph ~ .,
  data = train_scaled,
  method = "knn",
  trControl = ctrl_5fold,
  tuneGrid = knn_grid,
  na.action = na.omit
)

# Model summary
print(knn_model)

# Best k value
cat("\nBest k (number of neighbors):", knn_model$bestTune$k)
```

### 6.1.2 Hyperparameter Tuning Visualization

```{r knn-tuning}
# Plot tuning results
plot(knn_model, main = "KNN Hyperparameter Tuning (5-Fold CV)")

# Detailed view of k vs RMSE
ggplot(knn_model$results, aes(x = k, y = RMSE)) +
  geom_line(color = "steelblue", size = 1) +
  geom_point(color = "steelblue", size = 3) +
  geom_vline(xintercept = knn_model$bestTune$k, 
             linetype = "dashed", color = "red") +
  labs(title = "KNN: RMSE vs Number of Neighbors (k)",
       subtitle = paste("Optimal k =", knn_model$bestTune$k),
       x = "k (Number of Neighbors)", y = "RMSE") +
  theme_minimal()
```

### 6.1.3 Cross-Validation Performance

```{r knn-cv-performance}
# Cross-validation results for best k
knn_cv_results <- knn_model$results %>%
  filter(k == knn_model$bestTune$k)

print("KNN Cross-Validation Results (5-fold):")
print(knn_cv_results)

cat("\nKNN Cross-Validation RMSE:", round(knn_cv_results$RMSE, 4))
cat("\nKNN Cross-Validation R-squared:", round(knn_cv_results$Rsquared, 4))
cat("\nKNN Cross-Validation MAE:", round(knn_cv_results$MAE, 4))
```

### 6.1.4 Bias-Variance Tradeoff Analysis

```{r knn-bias-variance}
# Plot showing bias-variance tradeoff
knn_results_plot <- knn_model$results %>%
  mutate(
    RMSE_lower = RMSE - RMSESD,
    RMSE_upper = RMSE + RMSESD
  )

ggplot(knn_results_plot, aes(x = k)) +
  geom_ribbon(aes(ymin = RMSE_lower, ymax = RMSE_upper), 
              fill = "steelblue", alpha = 0.2) +
  geom_line(aes(y = RMSE), color = "steelblue", size = 1) +
  geom_point(aes(y = RMSE), color = "steelblue", size = 2) +
  geom_vline(xintercept = knn_model$bestTune$k, 
             linetype = "dashed", color = "red") +
  labs(title = "KNN: RMSE with Confidence Band",
       subtitle = "Shaded area shows ±1 SD across folds",
       x = "k (Number of Neighbors)", 
       y = "RMSE") +
  theme_minimal()
```

