## 6.2 Model 5: Ridge Regression

Ridge regression (L2 regularization) shrinks coefficients toward zero but doesn't set them exactly to zero. It's useful when there's multicollinearity among predictors.

### 6.2.1 Model Training with Hyperparameter Tuning

```{r ridge-model}
# Define tuning grid for lambda (regularization strength)
# alpha = 0 for ridge regression
ridge_grid <- expand.grid(
  alpha = 0,  # Ridge regression
  lambda = 10^seq(-4, 2, length = 50)
)

# Train Ridge model using scaled data
ridge_model <- train(
  ph ~ .,
  data = train_scaled,
  method = "glmnet",
  trControl = ctrl_5fold,
  tuneGrid = ridge_grid,
  na.action = na.omit
)

# Model summary
print(ridge_model)

# Best lambda value
cat("\nBest lambda:", ridge_model$bestTune$lambda)
```

### 6.2.2 Hyperparameter Tuning Visualization

```{r ridge-tuning}
# Plot tuning results
plot(ridge_model, main = "Ridge Regression: Lambda Tuning (5-Fold CV)")

# Log-scale lambda plot
ggplot(ridge_model$results, aes(x = log10(lambda), y = RMSE)) +
  geom_line(color = "darkgreen", size = 1) +
  geom_point(color = "darkgreen", size = 2) +
  geom_vline(xintercept = log10(ridge_model$bestTune$lambda), 
             linetype = "dashed", color = "red") +
  labs(title = "Ridge Regression: RMSE vs log10(Lambda)",
       subtitle = paste("Optimal lambda =", round(ridge_model$bestTune$lambda, 6)),
       x = "log10(Lambda)", y = "RMSE") +
  theme_minimal()
```

### 6.2.3 Coefficient Analysis

```{r ridge-coefficients}
# Extract coefficients at optimal lambda
ridge_coef <- coef(ridge_model$finalModel, s = ridge_model$bestTune$lambda)
ridge_coef_df <- data.frame(
  Variable = rownames(ridge_coef),
  Coefficient = as.numeric(ridge_coef)
) %>%
  filter(Variable != "(Intercept)") %>%
  arrange(desc(abs(Coefficient)))

# Top 15 coefficients by magnitude
print("Top 15 Ridge Coefficients (by absolute value):")
print(head(ridge_coef_df, 15))

# Coefficient plot
ggplot(head(ridge_coef_df, 15), 
       aes(x = reorder(Variable, abs(Coefficient)), y = Coefficient)) +
  geom_bar(stat = "identity", fill = "darkgreen", alpha = 0.7) +
  coord_flip() +
  labs(title = "Ridge Regression: Top 15 Coefficients",
       x = "Variable", y = "Coefficient") +
  theme_minimal()
```

### 6.2.4 Coefficient Path

```{r ridge-path}
# Coefficient path plot
plot(ridge_model$finalModel, xvar = "lambda", label = TRUE)
title("Ridge Regression: Coefficient Path")
```

### 6.2.5 Cross-Validation Performance

```{r ridge-cv-performance}
# Cross-validation results for best lambda
ridge_cv_results <- ridge_model$results %>%
  filter(lambda == ridge_model$bestTune$lambda)

print("Ridge Regression Cross-Validation Results (5-fold):")
print(ridge_cv_results)

cat("\nRidge Cross-Validation RMSE:", round(ridge_cv_results$RMSE, 4))
cat("\nRidge Cross-Validation R-squared:", round(ridge_cv_results$Rsquared, 4))
cat("\nRidge Cross-Validation MAE:", round(ridge_cv_results$MAE, 4))
```

